[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-40446"] :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type III region given by \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}\\le z\\le 2{x}^{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 2xz}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{2xz}2x\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{2xz}2x\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{2xz}2x\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}2x[y]_{y=0}^{y=2xz}dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}2x(2xz)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}4{x}^{2}z\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}4{x}^{2}z\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}4{x}^{2}z\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}[{z}^{2}]_{z={x}^{2}}^{z=2{x}^{2}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}((2{x}^{2})^{2}-({x}^{2})^{2})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{6}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{6}\\,dx & ={[\\frac{6{x}^{7}}{7}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-161707/selection/53f8483d0e775c7a968fb93ed0cf201007d0a92e13eebb5a96e0ec4f39f4dbe8" :answer/id #uuid "1435e028-99d2-5627-b830-911174be3e37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "92" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161707/selection/bc787d823ec953ec5e44b8f7f4a4c7f3b5de4a6a5f1cea9c5a660d6b5e6faac7" :answer/id #uuid "42f4146c-1875-5481-aa6e-e32e3c2c16b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "96" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161707/selection/c5fad6b1da11b9b990be9e0d2fcb83dfa156d8e05ce4b7ef6802ba6bbc66674b" :answer/id #uuid "00d55826-3190-5a37-a80a-04f64ab94c98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "98" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161707/selection/842947b00d8ffc5745884eed061ea57d57affe318d15d13be5c3612b41e13326" :answer/id #uuid "9e993d76-5d6e-5f57-bba0-265da0bc8945" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "84" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161707/selection/85a3108a003d23ae32c148d83b3c58c683299fe7f8b4da18365678303eb14a49" :answer/id #uuid "49840418-28a8-5eca-8345-fbb5b95e6529" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "88" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161707/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "27f1bac3-5478-5043-b94f-4b5e882a771d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161707/selection/bc787d823ec953ec5e44b8f7f4a4c7f3b5de4a6a5f1cea9c5a660d6b5e6faac7" :answer-field/choices ["q-161707/selection/53f8483d0e775c7a968fb93ed0cf201007d0a92e13eebb5a96e0ec4f39f4dbe8" "q-161707/selection/bc787d823ec953ec5e44b8f7f4a4c7f3b5de4a6a5f1cea9c5a660d6b5e6faac7" "q-161707/selection/c5fad6b1da11b9b990be9e0d2fcb83dfa156d8e05ce4b7ef6802ba6bbc66674b" "q-161707/selection/842947b00d8ffc5745884eed061ea57d57affe318d15d13be5c3612b41e13326" "q-161707/selection/85a3108a003d23ae32c148d83b3c58c683299fe7f8b4da18365678303eb14a49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161707" :question/id #uuid "99d7aeb0-f499-5945-8df6-2ed6bcdeb02c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161707" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{8}z\\,dy]dA\n$$\n\ngiven that the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 4}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}z\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}z[y]_{y={x}^{3}}^{y=8}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}z(8-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I region in the $xz$-plane.\nTherefore, to evaluate our double integral as a repeated integral over this region, we integrate with respect to $z$ and then with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}z(8-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}z(8-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(8-{x}^{3})[{\\int }_{0}^{4}z\\,\\text{d}z]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(8-{x}^{3}){[\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=4}\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}8(8-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8{[8x-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=2} \\\\  & =8(16-4) \\\\  & =96\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161707/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "40486856-137f-55c4-8464-f99e7e1c659f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161707"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161781/selection/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" :answer/id #uuid "9b3b0ebc-7d21-5c71-a721-332d43af1174" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161781/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "a78fa246-c089-53e2-a15c-5dbe923a5fb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161781/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "7a060360-f156-5748-aff7-a371cead9a02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161781/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "e1ea7d75-5311-56b3-82e1-01e10e2e95c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161781/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "a14914d8-167e-54df-abc7-7cd270fbff56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161781/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "71963b0e-cb06-5435-90a3-bd88b0dc18b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161781/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-161781/selection/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" "q-161781/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-161781/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-161781/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-161781/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161781" :question/id #uuid "62ec7383-3add-5783-838d-5ccce9844f89" :question/math-academy-id "q-161781" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}6y\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,x\\le y\\le 1-z},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $xz$-plane enclosed between the $x$-axis, the $z$-axis,  and the curve $z=1-x$ in the first quadrant." :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}6y\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{x}^{1-z}6y\\,dy]dA.\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{x}^{1-z}6y\\,dy]dA & ={∬}_{D}3[{y}^{2}]_{y=x}^{y=1-z}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3((1-z)^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe must now evaluate this double integral over the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/819b5b00967bf485068c146602bf962481b21b75d5319113fd6bd94366e84be0.png)\n\n \n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}3((1-z)^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,dA & ={∬}_{D}3((1-z)^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}3((1-z)^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-(1-z)^{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=1-x}-3{x}^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=1-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-{x}^{3}+1-3{x}^{2}(1-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\,\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-{x}^{3}+x]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(\\,\\frac{1}{2}-1+1)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161781/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4693bb81-f299-50fa-9cbd-3a5bb1c90da9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161781"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161853/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "23ab1ed5-f014-50fa-95a5-86d98fd53cc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161853/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "48018ee4-99b8-5569-8237-2eac9f1f6af5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161853/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "43e1218d-1686-5faf-a74d-aa659e7074f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161853/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "1ecea781-e9c8-5466-9fdd-87247b399b19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161853/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "1e172e0f-2815-58d5-876f-c1d82ada6dd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161853/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "64ab83e3-34fe-58d5-af51-8fbbc1cca887" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161853/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer-field/choices ["q-161853/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-161853/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-161853/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" "q-161853/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-161853/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161853" :question/id #uuid "86b32cbc-034e-5e5d-a572-7bdac44abc92" :question/math-academy-id "q-161853" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/a1e4a1e39c85a037f3f4f49910b651300363ef34bee969464f5e711aa00986e3.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}4{x}^{2}z\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/9165163be9ce95e7165f04d26e6ce8080699ab4d477eba3f804c849fdf1fb679.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/ca74bf149c1371fe9f1622586d9eb92fe180a9c9bb6a0c53d16f538b3c55f4a4.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-z}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}4{x}^{2}z\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-z}4{x}^{2}z\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-z}4{x}^{2}z\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-z}4{x}^{2}z\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4{x}^{2}z[y]_{y=0}^{y=4-z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4{x}^{2}z(4-z)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(16{x}^{2}z-4{x}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(16{x}^{2}z-4{x}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}(16{x}^{2}z-4{x}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[8{x}^{2}{z}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{2}{z}^{3}]_{z=0}^{z=3}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}36{x}^{2}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}36{x}^{2}\\,dx & ={[12{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(12-0) \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161853/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1889f67-327c-5e6e-b646-5bd58a244778"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161853"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163717/selection/80d1b63c012b48603c0fc8e4bbd16454b2c280a953986848782afca5b0c2471b" :answer/id #uuid "48c9c8fd-b99a-512f-9a57-971387f731a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163717/selection/7e9dc5d96566b0b22073848024fc142572bca10b8023dcd4f9bbc3f4b5ddf11a" :answer/id #uuid "1e7e04cb-4ca2-568a-bc6e-ca0b1558c1e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163717/selection/d2308954b066b666fe141e68f8c6fd40ad7633f5a0ca1cd9f42540e76f42c639" :answer/id #uuid "d6fd3211-7e10-5e56-a787-604f79b01d2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163717/selection/1dd779d99d88c78cc7fa6ab1f4ff23f6033ab8b1d94e8ec002629d7c33975708" :answer/id #uuid "ced0079b-bb9d-59e1-acda-9c6a3179d2e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163717/selection/40495612a66e54e83c500131ddc00640ec3ccf57ceafa3264aa25e473ed2be9a" :answer/id #uuid "577db99d-685d-5971-9333-5ba8fd225b0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163717/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9beacf14-34cf-50c2-82fb-15fe2d583a4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-163717/selection/40495612a66e54e83c500131ddc00640ec3ccf57ceafa3264aa25e473ed2be9a" :answer-field/choices ["q-163717/selection/80d1b63c012b48603c0fc8e4bbd16454b2c280a953986848782afca5b0c2471b" "q-163717/selection/7e9dc5d96566b0b22073848024fc142572bca10b8023dcd4f9bbc3f4b5ddf11a" "q-163717/selection/d2308954b066b666fe141e68f8c6fd40ad7633f5a0ca1cd9f42540e76f42c639" "q-163717/selection/1dd779d99d88c78cc7fa6ab1f4ff23f6033ab8b1d94e8ec002629d7c33975708" "q-163717/selection/40495612a66e54e83c500131ddc00640ec3ccf57ceafa3264aa25e473ed2be9a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163717" :question/id #uuid "98d947ff-3e63-571a-956d-fa65049b909f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163717" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/4be9362c014a7b8f0d0708ca5d7ea32a1b5bb13d48e2e1704341d04b89f9566a.png)\n\nGiven that $R$ is the type III region shown above, \n${∭}_{R}\\frac{\\pi x}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi y}{4}\\,\\text{d}V=$" :question/worked-solution "For a type III region $R$ with projection $D$ onto the $xz$-plane, the triple integral of a continuous function $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe consider the region $R$ as a type III region enclosed between the back surface $y={u}_{1}(x,z)=0$ and the front surface $y={u}_{2}(x,z)=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/63cffdee00edd80c4a0abdc30e8e45b1af29078b8bc4902bf3f60b7b4a104172.png)\n\nSo, the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type II *plane* region in the $xz$-plane with the right curve\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{ln}⁡z.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070114/assets/dc72aeb4b554d88f00083dc6bf6f8ca4244e1b7683c8dec10ba0491c678a5603.png)\n\nHence, $D={(x,z)\\,:\\,1\\le z\\le e,\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡z}.$\n\nTherefore, we write the triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{\\pi x}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi y}{4}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\pi x}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi y}{4}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}x[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi y}{4}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}x{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi y}{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-163717/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1889f67-327c-5e6e-b646-5bd58a244778"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163717"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
